@JonasVautherin good question. So I am in visual studio 2022 and the default shell is a developer powershell.

That path does look like it resolves to the correct absolute path of the mavsdk build/release/install folder

@julianoes I can definitely make PR's to the docs for the first two issues. For the dependencies that are not found, do you have time to schedule a call to walk me through what the issue could be? 

For python in windows, I don't know if it's version specific or just the python package from the microsoft store that causes the issue. I disable the app installer for python and manually install it from python.org and that is the current workaround at least for windows 11 and windows 10

